CEF's patches to Chrome whose behaviour NNCore relies on, kept when CEF left the tree (2026-10-09). From
CEF 8037's cef/patch/patches (BSD-3-Clause, Chromium Embedded Framework Authors), unchanged but for the
Windows-only parts and comments:
- chrome_browser_browser (only these parts): BrowserManagerService::DeleteBrowser reads what it needs before
  the Browser goes, since that can release the last reference to a private profile and destroy the service
  itself (private profiles released with their last Browser); and the tab strip API's colour provider
  tolerates a strip without an active tab (NNCore keeps Browsers with empty strips) instead of a CHECK.
- mac_keyboard_conversion_1467329: a key with no DOM key mapping is DomKey::NONE, not a fatal NOTREACHED.
- mac_platform_style_bubble_893292: bubbles near a screen edge are placed as the shipped builds placed them.
- screen_1443650 (ui/display/screen.cc): DIP <-> screen rects round instead of enclosing (the geometry the
  Dia measurements were taken on).
- mac_print_preview_modal: print preview's Save as PDF dialog keeps its file dialog policy, and a window with
  a sheet stays resizable.
- mac_chrome_locale_3623: the Mac UI locale comes from Local State, as on other platforms; LoadLocalState takes
  the ResourceBundle delegate (engine/nncore/apply.sh passes NNCore's).
- chrome_browser_extensions_background: browser_tests builds without background mode (gn gen asserts
  otherwise; the build keeps enable_background_mode=false, as CEF's build had it).
